 5/26/2019

 17:00-18:00 give up
 20:50- read editorial

 http://kmjp.hatenablog.jp/entry/2019/05/26/1330
 https://img.atcoder.jp/abc128/editorial.pdf

 I thought there are two cases
 1. k*A-k*B=N-1
 2. (k+1)*A-k*B=N-1

 However case #1 cannot happen. If happened, step is beyond N-1 😡

 There are two points

 1. Transform formula to upper-bound by multiple of two variables

 (k+1)*A+k*B=N-1

 2. Recurrence relation for # of steps



 */

const int MAX_N=1e6+1;
LL S[MAX_N];
int N;

void solve() {
  LL res=0;
  FOR(c,1,N-1) {
    LL cur=0;
    SETI viz;
    FOR(k,1,N-1/c) {
      LL a=k*c,b=N-1-k*c;
      if(b<=0) break;
      if(viz.count(a)) break;
      viz.emplace(a);
      if(viz.count(b)) break;
      viz.emplace(b);
      cur+=S[a]+S[b];
//      dump(c,k,a,b,S[a],S[b],cur);
      SMAX(res,cur);
    }
  }
  cout<<res<<endl;
}

